  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Devendra vs State Of U.P. on 16 March, 2023 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 85 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 5932 of 2023 Applicant :- Devendra Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Rakesh Kumar Verma Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "It has been submitted that implication under Section 272 IPC is unjustified since there is a special Act holding the field, i.e. Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. False recovery has been shown against the applicant. The offence under sections 60(2) of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate The applicant is in jail since 09.12.2022. On the other hand learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail but could not dispute the above submissions. Devendra vs State Of U.P. on 16 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171144569/ 1",
